## Sync checklist (every product update)

### 1. Read the product repo first

Pull these from the product repo `main` (GitHub API or clone) — do not guess from memory:

1. `style.css` / plugin header → **version**, requires PHP/WP, tested up to
2. `readme.txt` Stable tag + Description / FAQ (store parser truth)
3. `CHANGELOG.md` latest entry (user-facing “what changed”)
4. `README.md` marketing summary (features, install, fiction callout)
5. `BRAND.md` (if present) → tagline, palette hex, voice
6. `docs/marketplace/themeforest-listing.md` or equivalent listing copy
7. Latest commits / `theme-latest` release assets (confirm the zip version shipped)

Prefer **code + README + BRAND** over a stale listing file when they disagree. If `readme.txt` or ThemeForest copy still says “classic / non-block” but README and commits ship Gutenberg blocks, update the **matthummel catalog** to match the shipping product, and note the drift in the PR (do not silently keep the stale claim).

### 2. Map into `product-catalog.json`

Update only the product’s object under `resources/data/product-catalog.json`. Keep first-person / plain voice on matthummel (`master-content-writer.mdc`). Shop glossary: shops, agencies, developers, learners — not “clients” unless Matt already used it.

Required fields to re-check every sync:

| Field | Where it comes from |
| --- | --- |
| `version` | Product `style.css` / Stable tag |
| `compatible` | Requires at least + Requires PHP (+ tested up to when useful) |
| `summary` / `blurb` / `eyebrow` | README one-liner + audience |
| `approach` / `architecture` / `handoff` | How buyers actually edit (blocks vs metaboxes vs Customizer) |
| `benefits` / `deliverables` / `metrics` | Real features only (block count, color styles, GPL) |
| `faq` | Store FAQ + honesty (no live MLS/IDX unless true) |
| `demo` / `github` / `support` / `docs` | Live demo, repo, SUPPORT.md, buyer guide |
| `brand_tagline` / `brand_palette` | `BRAND.md` |
| `tech` | Accurate stack tags (e.g. Gutenberg when blocks ship) |
| `price` / `for_sale` / `live` | Only change when Matt sets price or visibility |
| `screenshots` / `image` | Paths under `resources/images/products/{slug}/` |

Keep `files_included` aligned with the marketplace pack (theme zip, child, Core, Documentation, Licensing).

### 3. Re-seed existing sites

Catalog JSON alone does not update published project meta after an earlier migration ran.

1. Bump a one-shot option in `app/concept-pages.php` (e.g. `mh_product_catalog_vN`).
2. Call `mh_apply_product_catalog(...)` (or the shared helper) with **force upsert** so meta + Woo sync refresh.
3. Wait until `mh_product_catalog_seed_data()` is non-empty before setting the option (in-place theme swap safety — same pattern as v2).
4. Prefer demoting non-catalog projects only on the first marketplace migration; later refreshes can upsert catalog slugs only.

### 4. Screenshots and assets

- Prefer the product repo’s `docs/marketplace/screenshots/` set (01–07 for Acreline).
- Convert / copy into `resources/images/products/{slug}/` as WebP when adding or replacing stills.
- Captions stay factual (what the screen shows). No fake “sold in 2 days” overlays.
- Featured image: `products/{slug}/featured.webp` unless the project already has a WP featured image (featured wins on cards).

### 5. Hardcoded fallbacks

If `app/concept-pages.php` (or similar) still has slug-specific audience / architecture / handoff for that product, update those strings to match the catalog so empty-meta fallbacks are not stale.

### 6. Docs and version on this theme

- `CHANGELOG.md` — user-visible product page refresh
- `docs/FEATURES.md` — mention the new catalog migration option if added
- `docs/MARKETPLACE.md` — only if marketplace submission guidance changed
- Bump this theme’s `style.css` Version when shipping the sync

### 7. Verify locally

```bash
ln -sfn /workspace ~/wp-site/wp-content/themes/matthummel
cd ~/wp-site && wp theme activate matthummel
# Delete the new option once if re-testing: wp option delete mh_product_catalog_vN
cd ~/wp-site && wp eval 'do_action("init"); echo get_option("mh_product_catalog_vN") ? "ok" : "pending";'
# Or hit /projects/{slug}/ and confirm version, benefits, FAQ, demo URL
vendor/bin/pint --test
```

Visitor-facing CSS/JS only needs `npm run build` if assets changed.

## Acreline-specific notes (reference implementation)

Synced from `matthummel-pa/wp-acreline` (Sept 2026):

- **Truth:** marketing pages are **21 Core Gutenberg blocks** (ServerSideRender, Block Generator, Migrate to Blocks). Listings / agents / bookings stay **classic metaboxes**. Customizer owns identity + eight color styles.
- **Version:** read `style.css` (e.g. 1.2.3). Demo: `https://acreline.matthummel.com/`.
- **Brand:** `BRAND.md` — tagline `Farms · land · historic homes`; paper `#f5f4f1` (not the older cream).
- **Honesty:** fiction demo, 555 phones, `@acreline-concept.test`, not a live MLS/IDX.
- **Do not** claim Elementor, ACF, or live IDX. **Do** describe Gutenberg blocks when the product ships them.
- ThemeForest attribute “Gutenberg optimized” in seller docs may lag the product — catalog copy should match the **shipping theme**, and call out listing drift in the PR.

## Future product themes

Repeat the same pipeline:

1. Add `{slug}` to `product-catalog.json` with the field map above.
2. Drop screenshots under `resources/images/products/{slug}/`.
3. Bump `mh_product_catalog_vN` (or extend the shared apply helper).
4. Add the repo to the table in this file.
5. Keep one primary CTA on matthummel.com (**Say hello** / buy on the product page) — do not invent a second funnel.

## PR shape

One concern per PR when possible: “Sync {Product} product page from {repo}@{version}.” Include:

- Version + headline feature changes
- Migration option name
- Note any drift left in the product repo’s own `readme.txt` / ThemeForest listing
- Local verify of `/projects/{slug}/`
